# Globs (relative to the suite cache dir) that must already exist when this case's
# CACHED pass runs, optionally prefixed "min=N " to require at least N matches.
# Checked, not assumed: this case proves that a chart fetched under CLUSTER
# credentials does not satisfy an anonymous run, which proves nothing at all if no
# such chart was ever fetched. The suite orders private-chart-bump first (see
# requires-case), and bump's cached pass is what fills these entries; a rename or a
# dropped case fails loudly here instead of quietly disarming the gate.
#
# The glob names the CHART and the count pins BOTH versions (each version is its own
# cache entry): "some chart is cached" would be satisfiable by any earlier
# remote-chart case, which is exactly the hollow precondition a review caught. The
# layout is charts/cluster/<instance>/<key>/private-app - the instance segment is the
# per-cluster scope (cluster API server + ArgoCD namespace).
min=2 charts/cluster/*/*/private-app
